{
 "thread": "ejqd_BBqK_M",
 "subject": "Unequal time coding and convergence errors",
 "messages_listed": 2,
 "last_activity": "2023-11-03T07:18:50Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "DJl1HdE8BAAJ",
   "from": "paul.tho...@gmail.com",
   "author": "12eeef275b63e690",
   "date": "2023-11-02T21:08:02Z",
   "subject": "Unequal time coding and convergence errors",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Dear Lavaan Users,</div><div><br></div>We are fitting a cubic growth model as follows and have unequal time points, so have adjusted as necessary. Given the large magnitude of the fixed coefficients of growth functions, this seems to be causing some convergence issues (Hessian Matrix errors as estimates close to zero) as the other estimated parameters (particularly variance terms) are particularly small. <div><br></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">model <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-style:inherit\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit\">&#39; i =~ 1*t1 + 1*t2 + 1*t3 + 1*t4 </span></span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">+ 1*t5 + 1*t6 </span>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\"><a href=\"https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/growth.html#cb2-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:inherit;text-decoration-color:rgb(108,117,125)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/growth.html%23cb2-2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792415284925000&amp;usg=AOvVaw092bzEuI2ovCUXxHjUZ44v\"></a><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit\">           s =~ 0*t1 + 2*t2 + 4*t3 + 8*t4 </span></span><span style=\"background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65);color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre\">+ 11*t5 + 14*t6 </span></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit\">           q =~ 0*t1 + 4*t2 + 16*t3 + 64*t4 </span></span><span style=\"background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65);color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre\">+ 121*t5 + 196*t6 </span></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit\">           c =~ 0*t1 + 16*t2 + 64*t3 + 512*t4 </span></span><span style=\"background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65);color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre\">+ 1331*t5 + 2744*t6 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;text-decoration-line:inherit;white-space:pre\">&#39;</span></div><div>To compensate, we have reduced the model proportionately, so that the spacing remains proportionately correct but the overall magnitude is much smaller. This seems to avoid this issue as variance estimates are no longer near zero.</div><div><br></div><div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">model <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-style:inherit\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit\">&#39; i =~ 1*t1 + 1*t2 + 1*t3 + 1*t4 </span></span> <span style=\"color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">+ 1*t5 + 1*t6 </span>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\"><a href=\"https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/growth.html#cb2-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"text-decoration-color:rgb(108,117,125);color:inherit;box-sizing:border-box\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/growth.html%23cb2-2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792415284925000&amp;usg=AOvVaw092bzEuI2ovCUXxHjUZ44v\"></a><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit\">           s =~ 0*t1 + 1*t2 + 2*t3 + 4*t4 </span></span><span style=\"background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65);color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre\">+ 5.5*t5 + 7*t6 </span></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit\">           q =~ 0*t1 + 1*t2 + 4*t3 + 16*t4 </span></span><span style=\"background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65);color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre\">+ 30.25*t5 + 49*t6 </span></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit\">           c =~ 0*t1 + 1*t2 + 16*t3 + 64*t4 </span></span><span style=\"background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65);color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre\">+ 166.38*t5 + 343*t6 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;text-decoration-line:inherit;white-space:pre\">&#39;</span></div></div><div><br></div><div>Is this strategy sensible or is there a better option please? Thanks in advance for any advise offered.</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "S1ZGziVeBAAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2023-11-03T07:18:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: Unequal time coding and convergence errors",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Orthogonal polynomial contrasts should help:<div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://psycnet.apa.org/doi/10.1027/1614-2241/a000044\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://psycnet.apa.org/doi/10.1027/1614-2241/a000044&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792415284928000&amp;usg=AOvVaw30G6q0bggIwfZzvHez48uw\">https://psycnet.apa.org/doi/10.1027/1614-2241/a000044</a></div><div><br></div><div>The R function contr.poly() is flexible, accepting a vector of “time” scores in case measurements are unequally spaced. It provides orthonormal contrasts, which are not only orthogonal but are scaled to each have SD=1. </div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Terrence Jorgensen<br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, November 2, 2023 at 10:08:02 PM UTC+1 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">paul.tho...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Dear Lavaan Users,</div><div><br></div>We are fitting a cubic growth model as follows and have unequal time points, so have adjusted as necessary. Given the large magnitude of the fixed coefficients of growth functions, this seems to be causing some convergence issues (Hessian Matrix errors as estimates close to zero) as the other estimated parameters (particularly variance terms) are particularly small. <div><br></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">model <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-style:inherit\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-style:inherit\">&#39; i =~ 1*t1 + 1*t2 + 1*t3 + 1*t4 </span></span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">+ 1*t5 + 1*t6 </span>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,59,79);text-decoration-line:inherit;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-s